hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1727","**\nNarrated to us ‘Ali ibn Ḥujr al-Sa‘dī,\nNarrated to us Ismā‘īl—meaning Ibn Ja‘far—\nNarrated to us al-‘Alā.\n\nAnd it was narrated to us Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd,\nNarrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad—meaning Ibn Qays al-Madanī—\nNarrated to us al-‘Alā ibn ‘Abd al-Raḥmān.\n\nAnd it was narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Bashshār,\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Ja‘far.\n\nAnd it was narrated to us Abū Mūsā,\nNarrated to me Muḥammad ibn Ja‘far,\nNarrated to us Shu‘bah—\nQālah Bundār: from al-‘Alā.\nAnd Abū Mūsā said: I heard al-‘Alā say:\n\nAnd it was narrated to us Muḥammad ibn ‘Abd Allāh ibn Bazīgh,\nNarrated to us Yazīd—meaning Ibn Zuray‘—\nNarrated to us Rawḥ ibn al-Qāsim,\nFrom al-‘Alā,\nFrom his father,\nFrom Abū Hurayrah (RA),\nThat the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n“There does not rise the sun on any day, nor does it set, that is more excellent or greater than the Day of Jumu‘ah. And there is no creature that is not terrified by the Day of Jumu‘ah except these two heavy ones: the jinn and mankind.”\n\n‘Ali ibn Ḥujr, Ibn Bazī‘, and Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd said: “on a day more excellent,” and they did not doubt.\n\n---"
